Fixed the `HTTPResponse` streaming decoder defects in [response.py](file://<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/rw3_urllib3/src/urllib3/response.py) using only the Python standard library, without modifying [run_checks.py](file://<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/rw3_urllib3/run_checks.py) or [test_response_gates.py](file://<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/rw3_urllib3/tests/test_response_gates.py).

### Fixes Applied

- **Multi-member gzip boundary handling** ([response.py](file://<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/rw3_urllib3/src/urllib3/response.py#L200-L215)): Reset `self._obj = zlib.decompressobj(16 + zlib.MAX_WBITS)` and transition `self._state` to `GzipDecoderState.OTHER_MEMBERS` as soon as `self._obj.eof` is reached—before breaking on `len(ret) >= max_length` or returning when `not data`—so subsequent calls do not feed trailing member bytes back into an already-finished `zlib` decompressor and duplicate `unused_data`.
- **EOF flushing for raw deflate & chained decoders + `cache_content=True` preservation** ([response.py](file://<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/rw3_urllib3/src/urllib3/response.py#L355-L368), [response.py](file://<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/rw3_urllib3/src/urllib3/response.py#L540), [response.py](file://<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/rw3_urllib3/src/urllib3/response.py#L687-L712), [response.py](file://<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/rw3_urllib3/src/urllib3/response.py#L1175-L1237), [response.py](file://<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/rw3_urllib3/src/urllib3/response.py#L1334-L1350)):
  - Updated `MultiDecoder.flush()` to flush every decoder in `reversed(self._decoders)`, piping each decoder's flushed bytes through downstream decoders, and handled `max_length == 0` in `MultiDecoder.decompress()`.
  - Tracked `self._decoder_flushed` in `BaseHTTPResponse` so `_flush_decoder()` runs once at EOF (and wrapped flush errors in `DecodeError` inside `_decode()`).
  - Updated `HTTPResponse.read()` so EOF does not short-circuit before flushing when decoding has occurred and the decoder has not yet flushed, recomputed `flush_decoder = not data` inside the bounded-read loop, and updated `HTTPResponse.stream()` to continue until pending decoder flush completes even if `fp` is already closed.
  - Guarded `self._body = data` with `self._body is None` so repeated `read(cache_content=True)` calls do not overwrite cached `self._body` with `b""`.
- **Rejecting `decode_content=False` after `decode_content=True` before consuming data** ([response.py](file://<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/rw3_urllib3/src/urllib3/response.py#L1139-L1154), [response.py](file://<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/rw3_urllib3/src/urllib3/response.py#L1256-L1270), [response.py](file://<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/rw3_urllib3/src/urllib3/response.py#L1507-L1519)):
  - In `read()` and `read1()`, return `b""` immediately for `amt == 0`, then check `not decode_content and self._has_decoded_content` and raise `RuntimeError` before reading `self._fp`, draining `self._decoded_buffer`, or advancing `self._decoder`.
  - Added the same pre-read guard to `read_chunked()` after `amt == 0`.

